# AdCoherent Labs - connected engine configuration (copy to .env).
# The engine package loads THIS file first (never overriding variables
# already set in your shell), then each layer repo loads its own .env:
#   CV-RULE_ENG-NLP/.env   (OCR settings)        - optional
#   rag-engine/.env        (DATABASE_URL etc.)   - already present
# Anything set here wins only if not set elsewhere; one file is enough
# for a fresh machine.

# ----- Layer 3: LLM providers (set the ones your tiers need) -----------
# Free / Hobby tiers (Qwen models served via OpenRouter's
# OpenAI-compatible endpoint - https://openrouter.ai/keys)
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# OPENROUTER_FREE_MODEL=qwen/qwen-turbo
# OPENROUTER_HOBBY_MODEL=qwen/qwen-max
# Optional attribution headers (OpenRouter app rankings):
# OPENROUTER_SITE_URL=https://adcoherentlabs.com
# OPENROUTER_APP_NAME=AdCoherentLabs

# Pro / Design / Enterprise tiers (Anthropic Claude)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ----- Layer 3: RAG store + SaaS data plane (Supabase Postgres) --------
# Direct connection string. Without it the engine still runs, but with
# EMPTY regulation retrieval (reviews lean on needs_review) - fine for
# wiring tests, not for real reviews. The SaaS integration (engine/saas.py:
# tier fetch, quota, run/finding persistence, audit) uses the same string,
# overridable separately via SUPABASE_DB_URL. Local stack: socat proxy
# 127.0.0.1:54322 -> supabase-db:5432 (container adcoherent-rag-db-proxy).
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:your-super-secret-and-long-postgres-password@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres

# Embeddings (local MiniLM; FAKE=1 gives deterministic vectors, no model
# download - tests/dry-runs only)
# EMBEDDING_MODEL_NAME=sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2
# EMBEDDING_DIM=384
# EMBEDDING_FAKE=1

# ----- Layer 1: OCR ------------------------------------------------------
# "free" = local OCR (PaddleOCR preferred) - the current default on EVERY
# product tier. "paid" = Google Vision (needs credentials; falls back to
# local on any failure).
OCR_TIER=free
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/path/to/service-account.json
